{
  "schema": 1,
  "about": "Conformance vectors for the Sede view stream. A B frame payload is a 16-byte network-order header (u8 version 1, u8 flags with bit 0 the last chunk and no other bit, u16 reserved zero, u32 image sequence, u16 chunk index, u16 chunk count = ceil(image length / 65520), u32 image length 1..2097152) and a body of exactly 65520 bytes for every chunk but the last. headers: accepted headers with their fields and the body length each must carry. header_refusals: headers refused with the given body length; check is the Python diagnostic name. streams: frames read in order on a downstream view connection; announce is a view.image J document, document any other J document, chunk a B payload whose body is the image bytes from offset for length, where image byte k is k mod 251. expect lists what the reader returns in order, or refused_at names the step that refuses and closes the connection. documents: control documents each direction must accept or refuse, in their closed sets.",
  "layout": {
    "frame_kind": "B",
    "control_frame_kind": "J",
    "refused_frame_kinds": [
      "E",
      "S"
    ],
    "frame_max_bytes": 65536,
    "chunk_header_bytes": 16,
    "chunk_body_bytes": 65520,
    "image_max_bytes": 2097152,
    "version": 1,
    "last_flag": 1,
    "credit_max_images": 2,
    "image_pattern_modulus": 251
  },
